   415	**V1's single window.** A9.6 registers one window. V1's configuration lists exactly one entry, authorized at the
   416	freeze. A successor window needs a release that lists it, authorized before it opens, in addition to A9.6's
   417	rotation registration.
   418	
   419	**Scope.** The protection covers relying parties who run an authentic verifier release whose trust configuration
   420	lists D's service keys. "Authentic" means authenticated distribution plus trustworthy release-authority behaviour;
   421	uncompromised key storage alone does not validate an authorization decision. Within this scope, a captor of both
   422	channel credentials who lacks release authorization cannot make a receipt under keys other than those listed pass
   423	V1. Such a receipt is INVALID when its window overlaps a listed window or starts at or before the configuration's
   424	`as_of`, and UNVERIFIABLE otherwise.
   425	
   426	**Limits.**
   427	- It prevents acceptance by those relying parties. It does not ensure that anyone detects or publicly exposes a
   428	  capture. It provides no issuer detection and no public visibility.
   429	- A horizon result means the keys are not yet covered. It is not proof of a takeover.
   430	- Release-key compromise is distribution compromise, already a stated boundary. A captor with both channels and the
   431	  release key can ship a release that lists its own keys. A release delivered to one party is not detectable by
   432	  others.
   433	- A stale trust file gives an honest new-window receipt `UNVERIFIABLE / TRUST_HORIZON`, a safe false reject until
   434	  the relying party updates. This cannot occur in V1, which has one window.
   435	- A8.3 and A8.5 supply no evidence for this property, and no formal model run supports it. Its evidence is the
   436	  check's construction plus prospective vectors (memo, Part 3, row 5), which are exit evidence once registered.
   437	
   438	**Change accounting.** This is a BROADEN, not a wording correction. C4 gains a third authenticated source for the
   439	key set, the release. The adversary text gains a protection, within the scope above. The scenario mapping's
   440	verdicts are unchanged; a fresh captor-key receipt is deliberately a newly rejected case. The signed bytes, the P8
   441	encoding, `A_sig`, the existing two-channel checks and every existing reason code are unchanged. The specification
   442	hash changes. Adding the listing to the cut order is a gate and scope change and is labelled as one (row 33). The
   443	changed sentences are rows 25–33 of A10.7.
