   169	## A10.1 "Existed no later than T" is chain time, not UTC — OWNER DECISION, NARROW-CLAIM (review A01)
   170	
   171	A9 says the bytes and signatures "existed no later than a time T fixed by Bitcoin" (A9:36-37; again at :114,
   172	:133 and in C5, :144). A9 also says that header times are chain-time proxies (C5) and that a finite UTC cutoff
   173	"requires an additional, explicit backward-skew assumption that V1 does not establish" (:444-446). The ordinary
   174	reading of "no later than T" is a real-time bound, which A9 does not support.
