   370	an additional author choice. (c) Extend presentation protection to arbitrary new receipts under captor-selected
   371	keys for every relying party, with issuer detection or public visibility; this needs a mechanism V1 does not have
   372	(for example a witnessed public log), and is not supported by this amendment. (d) Rule other text. **(e) Adopt (a)
   373	and add protection against key substitution: the trust-file service-key listing of A10.4.1**, with its ordered
   374	classifier and authorization closure, scoped to relying parties using an authentic, trustworthy release. This is a
   375	BROADEN; it adds mechanism (rows 25–33). Rows 15–16 take effect on (a) or (e); rows 25–33 only on (e).
