   260	  a signing algorithm or key was safe when it signed. The documentation names what a later examiner must supply:
   261	  an authenticated safe-before cutoff per algorithm and per key, compared against T with A2.1's chain-time
   262	  uncertainty (CODEX-REVIEW 8). A surviving PQ attestation slot prevents a P-256 break alone from supplying every
   263	  required attestation signature. An ML-DSA-65 cutoff and the classical slot remain; historical authority, per-key
   264	  custody and continuing commitment and history security remain assumptions. A PQ slot never removes the need for
   265	  a theft cutoff.
