   314	### 3.5 Verifier CLI and release-provisioning interface (instrument level)
   315	
   316	**Interface convention, not a verdict rule.** This subsection records how the conformance suite and the
   317	differential harness drive a verifier under test. It changes no verdict, reason or T, binds no production release,
   318	and gives way to the release artefact and release-signature format when those are decided (section 14.2 items 1,
   319	2). Both implementations of differential run 1 used it. [OWNER 2026-10-14, interface convention from diff-1,
   320	EA-01/EA-02/EA-03/EA-12]
   321	- **Invocation and compiled-in inputs (EA-01).** `CMD --trust <config> --bundle <bundle>`. The compiled-in trust
   322	  configuration hash and catalog (section 1, section 5) are provisioned for TEST by environment: the TEST release
   323	  record from `TESSERA_V1_TEST_RELEASE`, authenticated by the public key in `TESSERA_V1_TEST_RELEASE_KEY`, and the
   324	  catalog from `TESSERA_V1_TEST_CATALOG`. A config whose hash is not the one compiled by an authentically signed
   325	  release is refused (`TRUST_CONFIG_UNAUTHENTICATED`, no verdict).
   326	- **Request (EA-02).** The request (D4) is `strict` by default; `--request <value>` supplies any other value.
   327	- **Output and refusal (EA-03).** A verdict is one JSON object on stdout carrying the six stable fields, either at
   328	  top level or under `stable`, `result` or `report`; diagnostics may accompany it. A startup refusal is a nonzero
   329	  exit with the refusal code on stdout or stderr and no six-field object.
   330	- **Release checker (EA-12).** `CMD --previous <config> --next <config>` prints `ACCEPT` or `REJECT` for the release
   331	  invariants of section 5.
